/-
# Computing the rank of equations in a free group (Kourovka Notebook Problem 6.25)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.25 (G. S. Makanin): (Well-known problem.)
Find an algorithm for calculating the rank of coefficient-free equations in a free group. The rank
of an equation is the maximal rank of the free subgroup generated by a solution of this equation.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Computability.Partrec
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Reduce
public import Mathlib.Order.Lattice.Nat

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupEquationRankComputableKourovka6Problem25Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.25 (G. S.
Makanin). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700372 (`KOU-6.25`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A coefficient-free equation is a word `w` in unknowns `xᵢ` (`i : ℕ`), solved in the free group
`FreeGroup ℕ` (every free group of finite rank embeds in it). The rank of a solution is the rank of
the subgroup generated by the values of the unknowns occurring in the reduced word (a free group by
Nielsen-Schreier, read as `≃* FreeGroup (Fin r)`), and `equationRank w` is the supremum over
solutions (at most the number of unknowns). An algorithm is Mathlib's `Computable`, with input a
list of letters.
-/

/-- The rank of the coefficient-free equation `w = 1` over a free group, `w` a word in the unknowns
`x_i` (`i : ℕ`): the largest `r` such that some solution `x : ℕ → FreeGroup ℕ` generates, from the
unknowns occurring in the reduced word `w`, a subgroup isomorphic to the free group of rank `r`. -/
noncomputable def equationRank (w : FreeGroup ℕ) : ℕ :=
  sSup {r : ℕ | ∃ x : ℕ → FreeGroup ℕ, FreeGroup.lift x w = 1 ∧
    Nonempty (Subgroup.closure (x '' {i | ∃ b, (i, b) ∈ w.toWord}) ≃* FreeGroup (Fin r))}

/-- Kourovka 6.25 (G. S. Makanin): the rank of coefficient-free equations in a free group is
computable from the word. -/
def equationRankComputable : Prop :=
  Computable (fun l : List (ℕ × Bool) => equationRank (FreeGroup.mk l))

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive records that Razborov (1984) found an algorithm computing the
rank of a coefficient-free equation over a free group, the maximal rank of the free subgroup
generated by a solution. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems,
Problem 6.25 (G. S. Makanin); resolution: A. A. Razborov, On systems of equations in a free group,
Math. USSR-Izv. 25 (1985), 115-162 (the Archive prints 1984), abstract: an algorithm is constructed
that computes the rank of coefficient-free systems of equations; Kourovka Archive, Problem 6.25:
This was found (Razborov), https://doi.org/10.1070/IM1985v025n01ABEH001272.
-/
public theorem_wanted equationRankComputable_holds : equationRankComputable

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeGroupEquationRankComputableKourovka6Problem25Wanted
